KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ throwing conversion to a reference: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
__is_nothrow_constructible(T &, U) is evaluated as __is_constructible
(cpp_typecheck_expr.cpp): binding a reference may call a conversion
function, whose exception specification is not checked, so assertion 1
fails.
